{%- comment -%}
  Resolves a product's NON code — the join key between Shopify and the codes
  the design keys off (NON1 … NON9, SET, STOPPER).

  Order of preference:
    1. metafield custom.non_code   — explicit override, always wins
    2. SKU pattern                 — the live store's SKUs already encode it
    3. handle                      — last resort so nothing renders blank

  Live SKU shapes this has to survive (verified against the store):
    NON1-750-B, NON1-750-6, NON1-750-12   → NON1
    NON1-750-B-POS                         → NON1
    NON1-375-B                             → NON1
    NON-MIX6, NON-MIX6-STOPPER             → SET
    NON-SET-EVERYDAY / SPRING / SPICE      → SET
    NON-SET-STOPPER                        → SET
    NON-STOPPER, AUSPOS-STOPPER30          → STOPPER

  Sets are checked before stoppers, because NON-MIX6-STOPPER and
  NON-SET-STOPPER are sets that happen to include one.

  Each test is its own `if`. Liquid has no boolean negation of a `contains` —
  `sku contains 'X' and sku contains 'Y' == false` is a syntax error, not a
  negation, and it takes every template using this snippet down with it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign code = ''

  # A gift card has no NON code and never will. Its SKU falls through the
  # pattern matching below to `first`, which on the live store is the literal
  # string GIFTCARD40 — printed as the eyebrow on the gift card PDP, where a
  # customer reads an internal SKU fragment where the range's name goes.
  # Blank here means the eyebrow renders nothing rather than something wrong.
  if product.gift_card?
    assign code = ''
  elsif product.metafields.custom.non_code != blank
    assign code = product.metafields.custom.non_code | metafield_text | strip | upcase
  else
    assign sku = product.selected_or_first_available_variant.sku | default: product.variants.first.sku | upcase

    assign is_set = false
    if sku contains 'SET' or sku contains 'MIX'
      assign is_set = true
    endif

    assign is_stopper = false
    if sku contains 'STOPPER'
      assign is_stopper = true
    endif

    if is_set
      assign code = 'SET'
    elsif is_stopper
      assign code = 'STOPPER'
    elsif sku != blank
      assign first = sku | split: '-' | first
      if first == 'NON'
        assign code = 'SET'
      else
        assign code = first
      endif
    else
      assign code = product.handle | replace: '-', '' | upcase
    endif
  endif

  echo code
-%}
